      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Um... I really wish I could say it only happened when I was overtired. That would make more sense, right? Like maybe I just needed some rest and my mind was playing tricks on me. \n\nBut... gosh, I feel a little bad admitting this, because I really want to be doing better. Even when things calm down... like, I had a quieter few weeks recently where I was actually sleeping a lot more. I wasn't making any of those huge plans to fix up the whole shop or anything. I was really trying to just be, you know, normal and relaxed. \n\nBut... I still heard him. That man's voice in the garage. And... well, I still believed my husband and my boss were... tracking me. I know that sounds terrible, and I really don't want to think badly of them because they are good to me! I just... it didn't go away just because I was resting and feeling calmer. Does that mean I'm doing something wrong? I'm really trying my best to ignore it and just do my work, I promise.",
